{"index":3223,"node_id":"235eb85f-ab6b-45b6-8184-62b8fd4bdd36","parent":"17f4bcb3-233f-4fc8-b5a1-6cefabd8d35b","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791157725.772357,"update_time":1791157747.644155,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"Created the configurable-update scaffold on `main`.\n\nThe config lives at:\n\n`ChatMachines/Special Reports/SBE End-to-End Protocol and State Machine Specification/configurable-updates.yml`\n\nIts contract is:\n\n```yaml\nversion: 1\n\nlists: []\n\n# Example:\n# lists:\n#   - name: listA\n#     script: update-functions/A.js\n#     args:\n#       - arg1\n#       - arg2\n#\n#   - name: listB\n#     script: update-functions/B.js\n#     args:\n#       - arg1\n#       - arg2\n```\n\nSo execution is strictly sequential:\n\n```text\nlistA\n  A.js(arg1)\n  A.js(arg2)\n\nthen listB\n  B.js(arg1)\n  B.js(arg2)\n```\n\nEach JavaScript file exports one function, and the iterator invokes it exactly as `handler(arg)`. It waits for each invocation to finish before advancing to the next argument or next list. fileciteturn780file0L2-L5 fileciteturn781file0L2-L5\n\nThe manually triggered workflow is:\n\n`.github/workflows/sbe-report-configurable-updates.yml`\n\nIt accepts the config path, runs the iterator, and commits only changes under the SBE report root. fileciteturn782file0L2-L5\n\nCurrent `lists` is deliberately empty; `A.js` and `B.js` are only schema examples until we define the actual update functions and arguments.\n\nCommit:\n\n`3940bffcf91b1889883a61b3f97d3cf8c3d948da`\n\nVerified as current `main`. fileciteturn783file0L2-L5"}
