{"index":3248,"node_id":"a830ad3a-179d-4c1d-ad0c-0f3a6733c973","parent":"fecf86ca-7975-42b9-9237-c85706b78583","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791158092.231366,"update_time":1791158115.389201,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"Implemented the first configurable operation as:\n\n`update-functions/append-to-metadata.js`\n\nIts function signature is:\n\n```js\nappendToMetadata(fileArg, keyValueArg)\n```\n\nwhere:\n\n```yaml\nfileArg: \"01 Document Control/01 Document Control.txt\"\nkeyValueArg:\n  status: draft\n```\n\nIf `status` does not exist, it is appended to the embedded `metadata` object. If it already exists, its value is replaced. The function requires exactly one key:value pair per invocation and preserves the invariant `\"this\":\"metadata\"`. fileciteturn789file0L2-L5\n\nI also changed the iterator so each item in `args` is itself a positional argument list and is executed as:\n\n```js\nhandler(...args)\n```\n\nSo this YAML:\n\n```yaml\nlists:\n  - name: append-to-metadata\n    script: update-functions/append-to-metadata.js\n    args:\n      - - 01 Document Control/01 Document Control.txt\n        - status: draft\n      - - 20 PASS-FAIL Semantics/20 PASS-FAIL Semantics.txt\n        - reviewed: false\n```\n\nproduces:\n\n```text\nappendToMetadata(\"01 Document Control/01 Document Control.txt\", {status:\"draft\"})\nappendToMetadata(\"20 PASS-FAIL Semantics/20 PASS-FAIL Semantics.txt\", {reviewed:false})\n```\n\nin that order. fileciteturn790file0L2-L5 fileciteturn791file0L2-L5\n\nThe active `args` list is currently empty, so no report document was modified yet.\n\nLatest commit: `24a66802e936beba0858f415e4b1a6392cb0246d`"}
{"index":3249,"node_id":"bbb21d22-8662-4b7a-9c23-2dd9e3e51492","parent":"a830ad3a-179d-4c1d-ad0c-0f3a6733c973","role":"user","author_name":null,"create_time":1791158879.246272,"update_time":1791158918.811737,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":null,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"I want to segment the text file to make them easier to programatically update. The segmentation can be dynamic or static, but I needs to be tracked. Metadata will hold these values "}
{"index":3250,"node_id":"cff75e51-23b2-4144-b307-fb6694ef578e","parent":"bbb21d22-8662-4b7a-9c23-2dd9e3e51492","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791158893.152148,"update_time":1791158898.64021,"content_type":"thoughts","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"{\"content_type\":\"thoughts\",\"thoughts\":[{\"summary\":\"Designing segment metadata\",\"content\":\"I’m treating each segment as a tracked record with an identifier, content mode, and locator. Static segments can use fixed boundaries; dynamic segments should use stable anchors or matching rules so edits don’t silently misalign them.\",\"chunks\":[],\"finished\":true},{\"summary\":\"Designed segment metadata\",\"content\":\"\",\"chunks\":[],\"finished\":true}],\"source_analysis_msg_id\":\"1e41d837-9219-42b9-bc4a-4443bf1595c4\"}"}
